Swift demangling -- src/demangle/schemes/swift/
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The grammar, the demangling-tree node kinds, and the spelling rules are those of
the Swift compiler's own demangler (lib/Demangling/Demangler.cpp,
lib/Demangling/NodePrinter.cpp, lib/Demangling/Punycode.cpp and the
include/swift/Demangling/*.def tables), which is the only complete description of
the mangling that exists. The Python here is an independent implementation of that
algorithm, but it follows its structure closely enough to be worth crediting.

The Swift project is licensed under the Apache License 2.0 with the Runtime
Library Exception; see https://swift.org/LICENSE.txt.

================================================================================
Swift conformance corpus -- tests/conformance/swift-real-world.txt
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Part of this file is the mangled names from the Swift compiler's own demangler
test corpus (test/Demangle/Inputs/manglings.txt), used under the Apache License
2.0 with the Runtime Library Exception. The expected column was produced by
running a swift-demangle built from the swiftlang/swift main branch over them.
The rest is a stratified sample of the symbols in the shipped Swift runtime and
Foundation.

